WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.580
I got a little piece
of business to do here.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.820
As you know, we just did
a "Sirius Garage Show."

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.870
Yeah, that was fun.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.703
That was fun.

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:10.590
It was a lot of fun, I really
think I nailed it and...

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:11.940
Oh, I think we think
we all did a great job.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.230
Yeah, what? Do you have notes for us?

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.340
No, no, whatever.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.030
I think both of you will grow by doing.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.635
The more you do it, the better you'll get.

00:00:19.635 --> 00:00:20.468
What? (laughs)

00:00:20.468 --> 00:00:22.050
But you know, these
shows are made possible

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.370
as you know, by Chevrolet.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.203
That's right.
Yeah,

00:00:24.203 --> 00:00:25.110
and I have a little nickname for 'em.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.123
I call 'em Chevy.

00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:26.970
Oh, that's a cool nickname.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:27.803
Oh, that's great.

00:00:27.803 --> 00:00:29.400
I came up with that this
morning on the way in.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.408
Wow.
That's nice.

00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:31.241
I was driving my Chevy and I said,

00:00:31.241 --> 00:00:32.640
"Hey, we could call these Chevys,"

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.412
and anyway, they have this
amazing lineup of EVs.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:38.520
You know what EV stands for?

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.690
Electronic vehicle.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.130
Oh, I thought it was Evie.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.432
I thought it was electric vehicle.

00:00:42.432 --> 00:00:44.490
(laughs) Electronical is what I call it.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.780
Is it electronical?

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:46.613
Yeah.
No, it's absolutely-

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.700
It's electric.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.250
They have a great lineup
of electric vehicles.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.083
Okay, there you go.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.020
You're welcome for being here.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.200
And they have sponsored the shows

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.450
that we're doing at the Sirius XM Garage.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.283
That's really nice.

00:00:58.283 --> 00:00:59.116
That is nice.

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:00.840
And it was nice 'cause it's
an intimate environment.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.300
We get like, 30 people.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.520
30 people is barely an audience as far as,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.800
I mean, I've performed for
tens of thousands of people

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.633
in soccer stadiums all across Europe.

00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:09.466
Have you? No, you haven't.

00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:10.299
C'mon, no.

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:12.990
But these are nice,
intimate special shows.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.960
So to have Chevy there sponsoring us

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.030
to get the word out on their EVs,

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.640
that's electronical vehicles.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.840
Electric vehicles.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.520
I know, but I like my
way of saying it better.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.450
I know, but it's wrong.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.130
Everyone knows these Chevy brands

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.863
but do you know that they're
now available in EVs?

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.563
No I didn't know.

00:01:30.563 --> 00:01:31.396
What's that stand for?

00:01:31.396 --> 00:01:33.270
Electronic vehicles.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.470
Yeah, Chevy's gone all out.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.210
They've got electric charging stations

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.140
all over the place now.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:37.973
That's cool.

00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:39.330
Yeah.
Yeah, 'cause you know,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.110
if they didn't have that,
that'd be kind of a problem.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.820
But they do.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.720
They're everywhere.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.010
Well, I mean,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.750
if I had to throw in my two cents,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.340
I'd say Chevy is taking some

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.173
of their best known

00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:52.770
and most beloved nameplates electric.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.480
So it's not like some random cars

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.830
I've never heard of before.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.960
I'd say Chevy has EVs for everyone.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.610
They make electric vehicles for every kind

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.230
of life stage and every kind of budget.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.520
Depending on what you wanna spend

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.750
and what kind of car you're looking for,

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.430
Chevy's got the EV for you.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.020
That's the kind of thing I would say.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.990
What would you say off the
top of your head, Sona?

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:10.940
Let's switch one.

00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:14.970
(Matt laughing)

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:15.900
You like an EV?

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.733
I do.

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:20.220
I would say, you know,
Chevy is the brand you trust

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.380
and they are very available

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.544
and you can go get them.

00:02:23.544 --> 00:02:24.780
And guess what?

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:25.613
What's that?

00:02:25.613 --> 00:02:26.640
For Mikey and Charlie,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.540
your two kids?

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.373
Yes.

00:02:28.373 --> 00:02:30.510
I'm sure they have a great family car

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.343
that you could buy.

00:02:31.343 --> 00:02:32.176
Okay, good.

00:02:32.176 --> 00:02:33.570
I wish I knew which one, but-

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.890
Do they still have the Chevette?

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.390
Oh, Silverado.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.500
Man, what a cool name.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.333
That's the best.

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:40.470
Isn't that the coolest name for a vehicle?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.520
What you got there?

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.050
Silverado.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.040
Oh man.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:44.873
That's great.

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:45.880
Wish I was the voice of Chevy.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:46.713
(Sona laughing)

00:02:46.713 --> 00:02:47.640
Give it a shot.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.970
Silverado EV.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.803
[Matt] That's pretty good.

00:02:51.803 --> 00:02:53.853
If you want an EV, get a Silverado.

00:02:53.853 --> 00:02:57.389
Well now you're just like a smokin' wino.

00:02:57.389 --> 00:02:59.340
It sounds like you have an issue,

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.450
like a sickness.
(Matt laughing)

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.500
All right.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.333
Well, anyway.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.927
You sound like you're about to say,

00:03:04.927 --> 00:03:07.061
"Wanna know how I got these scars?"

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:07.920
(all laughing)

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.873
You're in a no smoking commercial.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.500
(Sona laughing)

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.880
Hey listen.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.390
Can I borrow your clothes?

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.754
(all laughing)

00:03:19.754 --> 00:03:21.423
I used to have pants.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.213
Chevy.

00:03:23.213 --> 00:03:24.330
You know, if I was listening

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.347
to this ad right now, I'd be saying,

00:03:26.347 --> 00:03:28.890
"Hey, in a very funny and charming way,

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.237
they've piqued my interest

00:03:30.237 --> 00:03:32.823
about Chevrolet's electronic vehicles."

00:03:32.823 --> 00:03:34.350
Yes.
Okay? Mm-hm.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.640
And I'd wanna know more.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.540
I'd say to learn more

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.600
about the all-electric Chevy EV lineup,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.580
head to chevrolet.com/conan.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.190
Make sure you're following @TeamCoco

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.870
for behind-the-scenes content

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.530
from these live shows and much, much more.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:54.030
And remember, my favorite
truck is the Silverado.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.997
'Rado, 'rado, 'rado.

00:03:55.997 --> 00:03:56.830
(Conan laughing)
That doesn't work.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.800
You know they have an
effect that can do that.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.461
Yeah, it's called, it's called me.

00:04:00.461 --> 00:04:02.040
(all laughing)

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.463
How do you think I got
started in this game?

00:04:03.463 --> 00:04:05.063
ado, -ado.

